                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/handle/20.500.12657/96025/9788898587056.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Focus on the underlying
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aiyalam+P.+Balachandran"}> Aiyalam P. Balachandran
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giuseppe+Marmo"} Giuseppe Marmo
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bo-Sture+Skagerstam"} Bo-Sture Skagerstam
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classical Topology and Quantum States
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/1180"} doi:10.1142/1180
          %p Other review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Skyrmions and QCD
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814503044_0010"} doi:10.1142/9789814503044_0010
          %blockquote
            %p
              If one assumes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%28N%29"} SU(N)
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              is equivalent to a theory of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              (and
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/glueballs"} glueballs
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constant"} coupling constant
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/N
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [..]
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              here to stress that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              is equivalent for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/N
              is the coupling constant,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} Large N
              is special only in that the meson coupling is only moderately weak.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [..]
            %p These considerations remove all of the obstacles to interpreting baryons as the solitons of meson physics
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [..]
            %p
              There is every evidence that Skyrmions physics with varying couplings reproduces QCD baryons of varying
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
